1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,775
Body Language Across Cultures.

2
00:00:02,725 --> 00:00:07,250
The same gesture communicates radically different meanings across cultures.

3
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:13,787
A thumbs-up signals approval in most Western countries but is offensive in parts of the Middle East and West Africa.

4
00:00:13,787 --> 00:00:20,650
Direct eye contact conveys confidence in Western contexts but can be interpreted as disrespectful in East Asia.

5
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:28,362
Personal space norms vary substantially: Latin Americans typically stand closer during conversation than Northern Europeans.

6
00:00:28,362 --> 00:00:35,675
The OK hand sign means fine in the United States but signals money in Japan and represents a vulgar insult in Brazil.

7
00:00:35,675 --> 00:00:44,887
Understanding these differences is essential in globalized professional environments where misinterpreted gestures can damage cross-cultural business relationships.

